{%- render 'glp1-assets' -%}
<div class="g1 g1-soft">
  <section class="g1-sec">
    <div class="g1-wrap">
      <div class="g1-split" style="align-items:center">
        <div class="g1-story">
          <div class="g1-eyebrow">Why GLP-1 hair falls out</div>
          <h2 class="g1-h2">It isn't a vitamin problem. It's a growth-phase problem.</h2>
          <p>A GLP-1 cuts appetite fast. The body reads that sudden drop in food as a famine, and in a famine it shuts down whatever it doesn't need to stay alive. Hair is 1st in line.</p>
          <p>So a huge batch of follicles leaves the growth phase at the same time and goes to rest. Doctors call it telogen effluvium. We call it the Famine Shed.</p>
          <p class="g1-pull">The hair in the drain today was switched off 2 to 3 months ago.</p>
          <p>That delay hides the cause. By the time the clumps show up, nobody connects them to the 1st months of the shot. And because the shot doesn't end like a crash diet does, the famine signal keeps firing. That's why so many women get a 2nd wave.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="g1-fig">
          <div class="g1-vt">From the Zepbound label</div>
          <h4>Same drug. Same trials. Women lost hair 14 times as often.</h4>
          <div class="g1-vbars" role="img" aria-label="Reported hair loss in the trials: women on Zepbound 7.1 percent, men on Zepbound 0.5 percent, women on placebo 1.3 percent.">
            <div class="g1-vbar" title="Women on Zepbound: 7.1%"><div class="g1-val">7.1%</div><div class="g1-bar g1-sw-a" style="height:83.5%"></div></div>
            <div class="g1-vbar" title="Men on Zepbound: 0.5%"><div class="g1-val">0.5%</div><div class="g1-bar g1-sw-g" style="height:5.9%"></div></div>
            <div class="g1-vbar" title="Women on placebo: 1.3%"><div class="g1-val">1.3%</div><div class="g1-bar g1-sw-g" style="height:15.3%"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="g1-vlabels"><div>Women, Zepbound</div><div>Men, Zepbound</div><div>Women, placebo</div></div>
          <p class="g1-cap">Reported hair loss in the trials. Source: Zepbound U.S. prescribing information (Eli Lilly), SURMOUNT-1 and -2 pooled.</p>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <figure class="g1-fig" style="margin-top:44px">
        <div class="g1-vt">The Famine Shed timeline</div>
        <h4>Nothing falls for 2 to 3 months. Then the whole batch lets go.</h4>
        <div class="g1-cycle" role="img" aria-label="Timeline: month 0 the famine signal, months 0 to 3 silence, months 3 to 6 the shed peaks around months 4 to 6, months 6 to 18 regrowth back to full thickness.">
          <div style="flex:0.6 1 0;background:var(--g1-deep)">Signal</div>
          <div style="flex:2.4 1 0;background:var(--g1-gray)">The silence: 2&#8211;3 months</div>
          <div style="flex:3 1 0;background:var(--g1-accent)">The shed: peaks months 4&#8211;6</div>
          <div style="flex:6 1 0;background:#c9b9c1;color:var(--g1-ink)">Regrowth to full thickness: 12&#8211;18 months</div>
        </div>
        <div class="g1-cycle-l"><div style="flex:0.6 1 0">Month 0</div><div style="flex:2.4 1 0">Month 1&#8211;3</div><div style="flex:3 1 0">Month 3&#8211;6</div><div style="flex:6 1 0">Month 6&#8211;18</div></div>
        <p class="g1-cap">Source: Cleveland Clinic (telogen effluvium); The Guardian, Sep 27 2026.</p>
      </figure>

      <div class="g1-cards">
        <div class="g1-card g1-step"><span class="g1-k">Step 1</span><h3>The switch</h3><p>A huge share of follicles leave the growth phase together and go to rest. Nothing falls yet.</p></div>
        <div class="g1-card g1-step"><span class="g1-k">Step 2</span><h3>The silence</h3><p>For 2 to 3 months, those hairs sit quietly in the scalp. The hair looks normal. The scale keeps dropping.</p></div>
        <div class="g1-card g1-step"><span class="g1-k">Step 3</span><h3>The shed</h3><p>The whole batch lets go at once. It peaks around months 4 to 6 and can run 3 to 6 months.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

